---
title: Portable Sandbox Snapshots
id: portable-snapshots
order: 10
description: "Keep completed sandbox files after the provider sandbox is gone, then rebuild them in a new sandbox."
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An agent can finish work in a sandbox, then the sandbox can disappear. A reload\nor a later run starts with an empty workspace. Portable snapshots store the\nfinished files in your persistence. A later run restores them into a new\nsandbox."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This work runs on the server. Your client calls routes that you own."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pick-your-path","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick your path"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start with persistence. Then add a product page only when you need that action."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required pages"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No persistence yet"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files come back after a reload"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-configure#create-new-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat persistence already"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files come back after a reload"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-configure#reuse-existing-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshots already wired"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A user marks one version"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-save","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save a Named Version"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshots already wired"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A user branches from one version"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-fork","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Branch From a Version"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshots already wired"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A product page that forks and compares two directions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-fork#see-it-in-the-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Branch From a Version"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshots already wired"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A user downloads a generated file"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-artifacts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send a Frozen File"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshots already wired"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The agent saves or forks this thread"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let the Agent Save and Fork"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshots already wired"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only some files, or one file"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick Which Files to Keep"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshots already wired"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Secrets, default excludes, restore safety"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a Snapshot Stores"}]}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic save and restore needs only the configure page. Save, fork, download,\nand file-policy pages are extra."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-a-checkpoint-holds","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a checkpoint holds"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After a successful terminal run, the middleware waits for persistence to save\nthe conversation. It then writes one checkpoint for the thread."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A checkpoint holds:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regular workspace files."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty directories."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generated artifacts that already belong to the thread."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The saved conversation for the thread."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File data and artifact data use separate content-addressed blob namespaces.\nEqual file data shares one file blob. Equal artifact data shares one artifact\nblob. Unused blobs stay until you delete them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-a-later-run-restores-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a later run restores files"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A later run restores the latest checkpoint only into a new private sandbox. The\nrestore runs after bootstrap and before hooks or the harness see the sandbox."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A live resumed sandbox keeps its current files. Portable snapshots do not write\ninto that sandbox. Provider-native snapshots make bootstrap faster. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle & Snapshots"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A named checkpoint stays available for a read or a selected fork. Automatic\nrestore still uses the latest checkpoint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The conversation comes from the durable message store. The sandbox journal is a\nrun-output log. When you need to replay agent output, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./journal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Run Journal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"who-calls-the-methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Who calls the methods"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSandboxSnapshots"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memorySandboxSnapshots"},{"type":"text","value":" return one object. That\nobject has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fork"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readArtifact"},{"type":"text","value":". Call those methods on the server\nafter you make sure that the session can access the thread."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not treat a checkpoint id, a thread id, or an artifact id as proof of access."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"pick-your-path","text":"Pick your path","level":2},{"id":"what-a-checkpoint-holds","text":"What a checkpoint holds","level":2},{"id":"when-a-later-run-restores-files","text":"When a later run restores files","level":2},{"id":"who-calls-the-methods","text":"Who calls the methods","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nAn agent can finish work in a sandbox, then the sandbox can disappear. A reload\nor a later run starts with an empty workspace. Portable snapshots store the\nfinished files in your persistence. A later run restores them into a new\nsandbox.\n\nThis work runs on the server. Your client calls routes that you own.\n\n## Pick your path\n\nStart with persistence. Then add a product page only when you need that action.\n\n| You have | You want | Required pages |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| No persistence yet | Files come back after a reload | [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure#create-new-persistence) |\n| Chat persistence already | Files come back after a reload | [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure#reuse-existing-persistence) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A user marks one version | [Save a Named Version](./portable-snapshots-save) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A user branches from one version | [Branch From a Version](./portable-snapshots-fork) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A product page that forks and compares two directions | [Branch From a Version](./portable-snapshots-fork#see-it-in-the-example) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A user downloads a generated file | [Send a Frozen File](./portable-snapshots-artifacts) |\n| Snapshots already wired | The agent saves or forks this thread | [Let the Agent Save and Fork](./portable-snapshots-tools) |\n| Snapshots already wired | Only some files, or one file | [Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files) |\n| Snapshots already wired | Secrets, default excludes, restore safety | [What a Snapshot Stores](./portable-snapshots-safety) |\n\nAutomatic save and restore needs only the configure page. Save, fork, download,\nand file-policy pages are extra.\n\n## What a checkpoint holds\n\nAfter a successful terminal run, the middleware waits for persistence to save\nthe conversation. It then writes one checkpoint for the thread.\n\nA checkpoint holds:\n\n- Regular workspace files.\n- Empty directories.\n- Generated artifacts that already belong to the thread.\n- The saved conversation for the thread.\n\nFile data and artifact data use separate content-addressed blob namespaces.\nEqual file data shares one file blob. Equal artifact data shares one artifact\nblob. Unused blobs stay until you delete them.\n\n## When a later run restores files\n\nA later run restores the latest checkpoint only into a new private sandbox. The\nrestore runs after bootstrap and before hooks or the harness see the sandbox.\n\nA live resumed sandbox keeps its current files. Portable snapshots do not write\ninto that sandbox. Provider-native snapshots make bootstrap faster. See\n[Lifecycle & Snapshots](./lifecycle).\n\nA named checkpoint stays available for a read or a selected fork. Automatic\nrestore still uses the latest checkpoint.\n\nThe conversation comes from the durable message store. The sandbox journal is a\nrun-output log. When you need to replay agent output, see\n[The Run Journal](./journal).\n\n## Who calls the methods\n\n`createSandboxSnapshots` and `memorySandboxSnapshots` return one object. That\nobject has `save`, `fork`, and `readArtifact`. Call those methods on the server\nafter you make sure that the session can access the thread.\n\nDo not treat a checkpoint id, a thread id, or an artifact id as proof of access.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Portable Sandbox Snapshots\nid: portable-snapshots\norder: 10\ndescription: \"Keep completed sandbox files after the provider sandbox is gone, then rebuild them in a new sandbox.\"\n---\n\nAn agent can finish work in a sandbox, then the sandbox can disappear. A reload\nor a later run starts with an empty workspace. Portable snapshots store the\nfinished files in your persistence. A later run restores them into a new\nsandbox.\n\nThis work runs on the server. Your client calls routes that you own.\n\n## Pick your path\n\nStart with persistence. Then add a product page only when you need that action.\n\n| You have | You want | Required pages |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| No persistence yet | Files come back after a reload | [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure#create-new-persistence) |\n| Chat persistence already | Files come back after a reload | [Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure#reuse-existing-persistence) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A user marks one version | [Save a Named Version](./portable-snapshots-save) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A user branches from one version | [Branch From a Version](./portable-snapshots-fork) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A product page that forks and compares two directions | [Branch From a Version](./portable-snapshots-fork#see-it-in-the-example) |\n| Snapshots already wired | A user downloads a generated file | [Send a Frozen File](./portable-snapshots-artifacts) |\n| Snapshots already wired | The agent saves or forks this thread | [Let the Agent Save and Fork](./portable-snapshots-tools) |\n| Snapshots already wired | Only some files, or one file | [Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files) |\n| Snapshots already wired | Secrets, default excludes, restore safety | [What a Snapshot Stores](./portable-snapshots-safety) |\n\nAutomatic save and restore needs only the configure page. Save, fork, download,\nand file-policy pages are extra.\n\n## What a checkpoint holds\n\nAfter a successful terminal run, the middleware waits for persistence to save\nthe conversation. It then writes one checkpoint for the thread.\n\nA checkpoint holds:\n\n- Regular workspace files.\n- Empty directories.\n- Generated artifacts that already belong to the thread.\n- The saved conversation for the thread.\n\nFile data and artifact data use separate content-addressed blob namespaces.\nEqual file data shares one file blob. Equal artifact data shares one artifact\nblob. Unused blobs stay until you delete them.\n\n## When a later run restores files\n\nA later run restores the latest checkpoint only into a new private sandbox. The\nrestore runs after bootstrap and before hooks or the harness see the sandbox.\n\nA live resumed sandbox keeps its current files. Portable snapshots do not write\ninto that sandbox. Provider-native snapshots make bootstrap faster. See\n[Lifecycle & Snapshots](./lifecycle).\n\nA named checkpoint stays available for a read or a selected fork. Automatic\nrestore still uses the latest checkpoint.\n\nThe conversation comes from the durable message store. The sandbox journal is a\nrun-output log. When you need to replay agent output, see\n[The Run Journal](./journal).\n\n## Who calls the methods\n\n`createSandboxSnapshots` and `memorySandboxSnapshots` return one object. That\nobject has `save`, `fork`, and `readArtifact`. Call those methods on the server\nafter you make sure that the session can access the thread.\n\nDo not treat a checkpoint id, a thread id, or an artifact id as proof of access.\n"}
